import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---
<DocsLayout
  title="Continuous capture"
  description="Three-layer passive capture: session stubs, opt-in external ingestion, and an append-only audit ledger with undo."
  current="continuous-capture"
>
  <p>
    Continuous capture is a three-layer system for passively recording what you
    work on. Layer A is on by default after install; Layers B and C are opt-in.
    All capture is local-first — no file contents leave your machine unless you
    configure an external source in Layer B.
  </p>

  <h2>Layer A — Session capture</h2>
  <p>
    A launchd job fires every 2 hours during work hours. It scans recent Claude
    Code session metadata and appends a one-line stub of what you worked on
    (working directory, file count, last git commit) to your private vault.
    No LLM call. No file contents leave the machine.
  </p>
  <p>
    Toggle via <code>/thinkos-autosave on|off|status|now</code>. Running
    <code>/thinkos-autosave now</code> triggers an immediate capture outside the
    scheduled interval.
  </p>
  <p>
    Source:
    <a href="https://github.com/dhirajsapkal/think-os/blob/main/docs/continuous-capture/session-capture.md">
      docs/continuous-capture/session-capture.md
    </a>
  </p>

  <h2>Layer B — External ingestion</h2>
  <p>
    Opt-in per source. Each source runs on a schedule:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Granola</strong> — hourly. Meeting titles and summaries from the last 90 days.</li>
    <li><strong>Google Calendar</strong> — daily. Recurring events for the next 14 days.</li>
    <li><strong>Linear / ClickUp</strong> — daily. Assigned open tickets.</li>
    <li><strong>Gmail</strong> — daily. Starred threads.</li>
    <li><strong>Slack</strong> — hourly. DMs and @-mentions.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Privacy routing: any content containing the keywords <code>comp</code>,
    <code>salary</code>, <code>HR</code>, <code>health</code>,
    <code>family</code>, <code>performance</code>, or <code>1:1</code> is
    routed to your personal hub only — never into a shared project vault.
  </p>
  <p>
    Configure sources via <code>/thinkos-capture-setup</code>. The command
    offers sources one at a time, safest first (Granola before Slack DMs). Each
    source can be toggled independently.
  </p>
  <p>
    Source playbooks:
    <a href="https://github.com/dhirajsapkal/think-os/blob/main/docs/continuous-capture/sources/">
      docs/continuous-capture/sources/
    </a>
  </p>

  <h2>Layer C — Audit ledger and undo</h2>
  <p>
    Every capture — regardless of source — appends one line to
    the vault note <code>90 System/Capture Log.md</code>. The ledger is append-only; it
    never modifies existing entries.
  </p>
  <p>
    <code>/thinkos-recent</code> shows captures from the last 24 hours, grouped
    by source. <code>/thinkos-undo-capture</code> removes any entry from both
    the vault and the ledger. Four new <code>capture:*</code> doctor checks
    report ledger health, source status, and any stale entries.
  </p>
  <p>
    Schema:
    <a href="https://github.com/dhirajsapkal/think-os/blob/main/docs/continuous-capture/capture-log-schema.md">
      docs/continuous-capture/capture-log-schema.md
    </a>.
    Audit model:
    <a href="https://github.com/dhirajsapkal/think-os/blob/main/docs/continuous-capture/audit.md">
      docs/continuous-capture/audit.md
    </a>.
    Top-level design:
    <a href="https://github.com/dhirajsapkal/think-os/blob/main/docs/continuous-capture/README.md">
      docs/continuous-capture/README.md
    </a>.
  </p>

  <p class="text-muted text-sm mt-12">
    Rendered docs coming soon. For now, the source files in the repo are authoritative.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
